From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Settings: storage sizes with the framework's unit strings

The storage page gave each category's size as "0.63吉字节" in Chinese
(Test V45): Settings' own FileSizeFormatter takes the unit from ICU's short
unit names, which are words in some languages. The page's total, formatted
by android.text.format.Formatter, already read "2.89 GB": on this device
that class takes its units from the framework's strings (kilobyteShort,
megabyteShort, gigabyteShort...), as in Android 9. FileSizeFormatter now
does the same; Android 9's version of it takes the suffix string as well.

--- a/src/com/android/settings/utils/FileSizeFormatter.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/utils/FileSizeFormatter.java
@@ -21,9 +21,7 @@
